{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 24.2% a year from $1.70 billion in FY2016 to $12.0 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F196]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 step change, revenue up 49.1% to $6.21 billion, came from the U.S. launch of TRIKAFTA in the fourth quarter of 2019 and KAFTRIO in the E.U. in the third quarter of 2020 [F5][D194][P51]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2024 broke the pattern: operating income fell to a $233 million loss on $4.6 billion of AIPR&D, including $4.4 billion for Alpine [F24][P11]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 recovered to $4.17 billion of operating income, but revenue growth slowed to 8.9% [F25][D446]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "TRIKAFTA/KAFTRIO contributed 13.1pp of FY2024's 11.7% revenue growth and only 0.7pp of FY2025's 8.9% [D528][D402][D531][D446]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "ALYFTREK, launched in FY2025, added 7.6pp of growth and 7.0% of revenue [D590][D589]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 net product revenues rose $950.5 million, or 9%, on continued growth, with ALYFTREK sales absent a year earlier [P3][S39][S69]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew faster than revenue over the window, at a 95.6% CAGR against 24.2% [F197][F196]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS rose to $15.32 in FY2025 from $13.89 in FY2023 while the diluted share count was flat at 258.0 million [F75][F73][X137]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 operating margin of 34.8% sits above the 31.8% window median but below the 48.2% FY2022 high [F35][D663][D662]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The 36.9pp FY2025 margin recovery was mostly the absence of FY2024's AIPR&D, a 37.7pp residual effect [D452][D468]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cost of revenue held at 13.8% of revenue in FY2025 as a lower overall royalty rate for CF medicines offset other costs [D425][P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "SG&A rose 19.7% in FY2025, costing 1.3pp of margin, as commercial spend outgrew revenue [D456][D467]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 net margin of -4.9% diverged from operating margin because the 315.5% effective tax rate reflected non-deductible Alpine AIPR&D [F54][D390][P5]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow was $3.63 billion in FY2025, primarily from $4.17 billion of income from operations [F85][F25][P1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $3.19 billion was 26.6% of revenue, below the 32.8% window median [F105][D431][D669]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow covered only 0.81x of net income, against a 1.07x window median and a 1.11x peer median [D435][D675][D694]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 47.0% to $438 million, 2.09x D&A and 3.6% of revenue [D447][F95][D436][D430]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash of $12.3 billion equals 102.7% of revenue, in the 88th percentile of eight biopharma peers whose median is -50.7% [D439][D440][D691][D692]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cash and investments rose 9.8% in FY2025, primarily on increased cash and marketable securities from product revenue [D460][P2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $2.02 billion absorbed 63.2% of free cash flow in FY2025, yet the diluted share count was unchanged [D441][D442][D459]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio of 2.90x is below the 3.52x window median [F185][D678]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Days inventory outstanding rose 85 days to 373 in FY2025, up from 287 in FY2024 [D444][D397]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Inventory has grown faster than revenue for several years, tying up cash and raising write-down risk if demand shifts [D462][D446]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The effective tax rate fell 300.7pp to 14.9% in FY2025 from the distorted 315.5% FY2024 rate [D433][D390]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "That swing is benign, reflecting FY2024's non-deductible Alpine charge rather than a change in the underlying tax position [P5]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
